{%- set faqs = [
  ["What cybersecurity services do technology and SaaS companies need?", "Technology and SaaS companies benefit from application penetration testing and API security testing alongside vulnerability assessment and penetration testing (VAPT), cloud security assessments, secure code reviews and network security testing. These services help identify vulnerabilities and protect customer data across software applications and supporting infrastructure."],
  ["Why is cybersecurity important for SaaS companies?", "Cybersecurity helps SaaS companies protect customer information and prevent unauthorized access while maintaining application availability and business continuity. Strong security controls also help build customer trust and address enterprise security requirements."],
  ["What is SaaS security testing?", "SaaS security testing evaluates the security of software-as-a-service platforms by identifying vulnerabilities in authentication and authorization alongside tenant isolation and data access controls. It helps uncover weaknesses that could expose customer information or allow unauthorized access to platform resources."],
  ["How does API penetration testing protect technology companies?", "API penetration testing identifies vulnerabilities in API endpoints and authentication mechanisms alongside authorization controls and business logic. It helps prevent unauthorized data access and privilege escalation while reducing the risk of API exploitation."],
  ["What is included in VAPT for technology companies?", "Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing (VAPT) involves identifying security weaknesses and validating their exploitability through controlled testing. Depending on the agreed scope, assessments can cover web applications and APIs alongside networks and cloud infrastructure."],
  ["How can technology companies secure their cloud infrastructure?", "Technology companies can strengthen cloud security by reviewing access permissions and configuration settings alongside network exposure and storage security. Regular cloud security assessments help identify misconfigurations and excessive privileges that could expose sensitive data or production workloads."],
  ["How does secure code review improve software security?", "Secure code review examines application source code to identify insecure coding practices and vulnerabilities involving input validation and authentication alongside access controls and sensitive data handling. Addressing these issues during development can reduce the risk of security flaws reaching production."],
  ["Can cybersecurity testing support ISO 27001 and SOC 2 requirements?", "Yes. Cybersecurity assessments can help identify technical vulnerabilities and control weaknesses relevant to ISO 27001 and SOC 2 security objectives. However, penetration testing alone does not establish compliance or replace formal certification and independent audits."],
  ["How often should SaaS companies conduct security assessments?", "SaaS companies should conduct security assessments at planned intervals and after significant application or infrastructure changes. Additional testing is advisable after major releases or architecture changes and when new vulnerabilities could affect exposed systems."],
  ["Does CipherTrivia provide AI application and agent security testing?", "CipherTrivia can assess AI-powered applications and agent-based workflows for risks such as prompt injection and insecure tool execution alongside excessive permissions and sensitive data exposure. Testing scope depends on the application's architecture and the AI components being evaluated."],
  ["What do companies receive after a cybersecurity assessment?", "Companies receive a security assessment report describing identified vulnerabilities and their severity alongside technical evidence and remediation recommendations. Retesting can also be performed within the agreed scope to verify that reported security issues have been resolved."],
  ["How can a technology company get started with CipherTrivia?", "Technology and SaaS companies can contact CipherTrivia to discuss their application architecture and security objectives alongside their testing requirements. Based on the agreed scope, the team can recommend relevant security assessments and define the engagement process."]
